<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xi Jinping</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xi Jinping is a Chinese politician who has been general secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> since 2012 and president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> since 2013. The son of the revolutionary leader Xi Zhongxun, he has concentrated power to a degree not seen since Mao, led a sweeping anti-corruption campaign and removed the presidential term limit in 2018. He began a third term as party leader in 2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xi-jinping.jpg" alt="Xi Jinping" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simon Dawson / No 10 Downing Street · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_visits_China_(55066713683)_(cropped%2Bangle).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
